  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises to adopt new business models, technology and techniques to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A network of 15 private trainers has introduced new support services for women entrepreneurs, offering targeted technical skills training as well as advice and coaching for women in areas where economic opportunities have been identified. 

An established network of 18 trainers from four different public institutions and NGOs offered the &quot;Women do Business&quot; training package to support women entrepreneurs in starting and growing a small business. In collaboration with the trainer network, ILO conducted a comprehensive assessment to identify economic opportunities for women. ILO then organized capacity building measures to develop the knowledge and skills of selected private trainers to enable them to monitor and advise women entrepreneurs. ILO supported the established network of trainers in training of 100 women entrepreneurs.

ILO adapted its tested training package &quot;Women do Business&quot; to the Jordanian context and trained 18 trainers from 4 public institutions and NGOs on the training content. ILO then supported trainers and partner organizations in training 225 female entrepreneurs, resulting in 125 women that established their own small business or expanded the existing ones to access new market opportunities.</narrative>
   </description>
